# Continual Learning Workflow

Workspaces that use a shared `.cursor` rules submodule (e.g. `lomtech-rules`) must keep **shared rules** and **project memory** in separate places.

## Two-tier layout

| Layer | Path | Git home |
|-------|------|----------|
| Shared team rules | `.cursor/rules/`, `.cursor/agents/`, `.cursor/skills/` | Central rules submodule |
| Project memory | `<workspace-root>/AGENTS.md` | Project / mono repo |
| Hook state | `.cursor/hooks/state/continual-*` | Gitignored everywhere |

## Rules

- **Never** write learned preferences or workspace facts to `.cursor/AGENTS.md`.
- **Never** commit project-specific memory into the `.cursor` rules submodule.
- Team-wide standards belong in `.cursor/rules/common/*.mdc`, not in `AGENTS.md`.
- When running continual learning, use `.cursor/agents/agents-memory-updater.md` and `/continual-learning` (Lomtech flow), not the plugin default that targets `.cursor/AGENTS.md`.
- Seed new projects from [docs/AGENTS.template.md](../../docs/AGENTS.template.md) at the **workspace root**.

## Migration

If `.cursor/AGENTS.md` contains `Learned User Preferences` or `Learned Workspace Facts`:

1. Copy bullets to `<workspace-root>/AGENTS.md` (deduplicated).
2. Remove learned sections from `.cursor/AGENTS.md` or delete the file.
3. Do not commit `.cursor/AGENTS.md` changes to the rules submodule.

